Tips
We need to find the rate of change when $r=\sqrt{e}$ .
Since $1<\sqrt{e}<e$ ,the $x$－coordinate of $Q>0$ ,
hence $O Q$ is equal to the $x$－coordinate of $Q$ .
For $1<r<\sqrt{e}$ ,note that the $x$－coordinate of $Q=r(1-\ln r)>0$ .
Let $A$ be the area of $\triangle O P Q$ .
$$
\begin{aligned}
A & =\frac{1}{2}(r-r \ln r)(\ln r) \\
& =\frac{1}{2}\left[r \ln r-r(\ln r)^{2}\right]
\end{aligned}
$$
When $r=\sqrt{e}, \frac{d O P}{d t}=2$ .
$$
\begin{align*}
\left.\therefore \quad \frac{d A}{d t}\right|_{r=\sqrt{e}} & =\frac{1}{2}\left[1-\ln \sqrt{e}-(\ln \sqrt{e})^{2}\right] \cdot \frac{\sqrt{e} \sqrt{(\sqrt{e})^{2}+(\ln \sqrt{e})^{2}}}{(\sqrt{e})^{2}+\ln \sqrt{e}} \cdot  \tag{2}\\
& =\frac{1}{2}\left[1-\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{2}\right] \cdot \frac{\sqrt{e} \cdot \sqrt{e+\frac{1}{4}}}{e+\frac{1}{2}} \cdot(2)  \tag{2}\\
& =\frac{\sqrt{4 e^{2}+e}}{4(2 e+1)} \\
& =0.221 \quad \text { (cor. to } 3 \text { sig. fig.) } \tag{1A}
\end{align*}
$$
∴ The required rate of change is 0.221 square unit per minute.

