(b) （i）Let $A$ square units be the area of $\triangle O P Q$ .
$$
\begin{align*}
& A=\frac{1}{2} p\left[\sqrt{(p-10)^{2}+9}+\sqrt{p^{2}+4}\right]  \tag{1 M}\\
& \frac{d A}{d p}=\frac{1}{2} p\left[\frac{p-10}{\sqrt{(p-10)^{2}+9}}+\frac{p}{\sqrt{p^{2}+4}}\right]+\frac{1}{2}\left[\sqrt{(p-10)^{2}+9}+\sqrt{p^{2}+4}\right]  \tag{1 M}\\
