(ii) Since $O P=\sqrt{p^{2}+\left(-\sqrt{p^{2}+4}\right)^{2}}$ ,we have $O P=\sqrt{2 p^{2}+4}$ .
At time $t$ seconds,we have $\frac{d O P}{d t}=\frac{2 p}{\sqrt{2 p^{2}+4}}\left(\frac{d p}{d t}\right)$ .
As $2=\frac{2(4)}{\sqrt{2\left(4^{2}\right)+4}}\left(\left.\frac{d p}{d t}\right|_{p=4}\right)$ ,we have $\left.\frac{d p}{d t}\right|_{p=4}=\frac{3}{2}$ .
Let $w$ units be the perimeter of $\triangle O P Q$ .
$$
\begin{align*}
& w=O P+O Q+P Q=O P+\sqrt{p^{2}+(p-10)^{2}+9}+P Q  \tag{1 M}\\
& \frac{d w}{d t}=\frac{d O P}{d t}+\left[\frac{p+(p-10)}{\sqrt{p^{2}+(p-10)^{2}+9}}+\frac{d P Q}{d p}\right]\left(\frac{d p}{d t}\right)  \tag{1M}\\
& \left.\therefore \quad \frac{d w}{d t}\right|_{p=4}=2+\left(\frac{-2}{\sqrt{61}}+0\right)\left(\frac{3}{2}\right)=2-\frac{3 \sqrt{61}}{61}
\end{align*}
$$
Thus,the required rate of change is $\left(2-\frac{3 \sqrt{61}}{61}\right)$ units per second.
